“Plan B is birch ply, one-sixteenth inch, painted to match the brick. A crow would recognize its own reflection in that smooth surface; they use mirrors to cache food where they can’t see later.”

She blinks. “I’m sorry, what?”

Jago doesn’t look up;

“Understood. You could use paper tape instead; American crows craft tools from twigs and can remember human faces.” She clipped the tape with a snip that sounded like small shears.

“Paper tape works fine. What about primer before painting?”

